# M11.5e: one result requirement is one written description, supplied by position, `:=`, or an ordinary field of
# one whole descriptor DATA. p1, p2 and p3 all require `@: c.FILE`; a copy of each
# (merge with one more field) shows the same part return: a reference to that written type form. The executors run
# only int results, so none of the three is called here.
# M11 5v: the copies are constructed in own data; final root references only
# expose their full contents. M8 keeps the explicit groups of p3, whose
# unnamed args/code targets therefore print as complete blocks.
fn: p1 (int: a) @: c.FILE
    return: 0
fn: name := p2; args := (int: a); return := (@: c.FILE); code := (return: 0)
fn: (name: p3; args: (int: a); return: (@: c.FILE); code: (return: 0))
sub: main () (
    @: R1 merge(p1; (int: zz 1))
    @: R2 merge(p2; (int: zz 2))
    @: R3 merge(p3; (int: zz 3))
) ()
main()
@: observed_R1 main\data\R1
@: observed_R2 main\data\R2
@: observed_R3 main\data\R3
